{:paths ["src" "test"]
 ;; Rank 3: the application, the top of the ladder — it holds the front end,
 ;; so it sits above the component backend (`tui`, rank 2) the widgets build
 ;; on. Its sources require only lower-ranked modules (kmet.srce.*,
 ;; kmet.libs.*, kmet.ai.*, kmet.loader.*, kmet.tui.*, kmet.reakt.*), plus
 ;; third-party code; the module may never require a module at its own rank or
 ;; above. babashka/process is the version rule's git describe.
 ;;
 ;; The front end lives here too (it was the `ui` module, rank 3, until it
 ;; merged). `modules/app/src/kmet/ui` holds the TUI's widgets, selectors and
 ;; mode row as `kmet.ui.*`, and the tool renderers keep their pre-rename
 ;; `kmet.agent.ui.*` names because shipped extensions require them by name.
 ;; A namespace prefix no longer marks the module, so the app/front-end split
 ;; is a path rule in test_layer_guard.clj: the business subtree
 ;; (`kmet/app/**`) may not require `kmet.ui.**`, `kmet.tui.**`, `kmet.tk.**`
 ;; or a mode row.
 ;;
 ;; Every namespace here is `kmet.app.*`. The lifts of 4c/4f/5l/7a moved files
 ;; and kept their `kmet.agent.*` names while kmet1 and kmet2 shared a module
 ;; tree; landing 11's pass renamed them with the subtree they belong to, so the
 ;; name follows the module now. The one exception is `kmet.extension`, the
 ;; extension ABI, whose name is its contract.
 ;;
 ;; The session layer (kmet.app.session.*, moved at 4c-i), kmet.app.registry
 ;; (landing 3), the tool layer (`kmet.app.tools.*`, moved at 4f in five
 ;; steps), and the host's leaf dependencies (kmet.app.debug, .config-schema,
 ;; .event-bus, .tools.util) were lifted ahead of the extension host's own move
 ;; so its requires stop pointing upward (new-app.md, 4b-ii). 5l-i closed the
 ;; session pair the front ends read: kmet.app.session.driver (the engine's
 ;; operations, retired with the handle migration) and
 ;; kmet.app.commands.builtins (the portable slash commands) — the driver
 ;; reached only what was already here.
 ;;
 ;; kmet.app.loop.stages is 7a's first step: the loop's stage map (`defaults`,
 ;; `for-ctx`, `refresh!`, and `with-defaults` for the ctx builders), so the
 ;; loop reads its stages from the ctx it was handed and
 ;; the loop reaches `kmet.app.loop-guard`/`.retry`, which live here.
 ;;
 ;; 7a's third and fourth steps moved the loop cluster as-is (namespaces kept,
 ;; tests to follow): kmet.app.loop.message, .loop.state, .loop.completion,
 ;; .loop.tool-exec, .compaction.core, .compaction.stage and kmet.app.loop
 ;; itself. They reach only what is already here or below, so the only source
 ;; left in `agent` that the loop cannot take is the Engine — its edges are
 ;; policy (command expansion, resource loading, the prompt wrapper) and move
 ;; with the modes.
 ;;
 ;; 7a's second step brought three leaves the loop cluster reaches for, moved
 ;; with no call-site edits because nothing in them reaches upward:
 ;; kmet.app.model-resolver (ai only), .project-context (no deps) and
 ;; .git-packages (fs/process, which this module already declares). They join
 ;; the session layer and the tool layer here.
 ;;
 ;; The prompt builder and the `:systemPrompt` row that provides it are one
 ;; namespace (kmet.app.system-prompt): the builder takes no registry of its
 ;; own, so an engine composes its prompt from the ctx it holds, and the row is
 ;; what fills the one input a service owns (kmet.app.skills/build-system-prompt
 ;; is kmet1's process-bound wrapper).
 ;;
 ;; The session layer brings the library edges it uses: libs for fs/edn-store,
 ;; ai for the usage tallies, and the two Maven siblings those need. The tool
 ;; layer added sci (its sandbox mints contexts); every other edge it needed was
 ;; already here. The host added kmet/hikap: its ABI registers tag aliases.
 ;;
 ;; 4b-ii-b brought the extension host's leaves, and then the host: the
 ;; isolated
 ;; evaluation context (extensions/context.cljc) and the host itself
 ;; (extensions/core.cljc, whose services arrive as a bound value so it needs
 ;; nothing from `agent`) require kmet.loader.*, the
 ;; bundled library set (extensions/libs.clj) is what makes those six
 ;; coordinates app's, and the loop's two stages (kmet.app.retry,
 ;; .loop-guard) came with them because they reach nothing above app. The pins
 ;; match the root deps.edn / bb.edn ones; kmet.test-module-deps holds every
 ;; manifest to one coordinate.
 :deps {kmet/libs {:local/root "../libs"}
        kmet/hikap {:local/root "../hikap"}
        kmet/srce {:local/root "../srce"}
        kmet/ai {:local/root "../ai"}
        kmet/loader {:local/root "../loader"}
        ;; The front end's component backends, from the merge: kmet.ui.* builds
        ;; on the TUI backend (which brings jline and, through hikap, reakt).
        kmet/tui {:local/root "../tui"}
        kmet/reakt {:local/root "../reakt"}
        babashka/fs {:mvn/version "0.5.34"}
        babashka/process {:mvn/version "0.6.25"}
        metosin/malli {:mvn/version "0.20.1"}
        ;; The bundled extension set (kmet.app.extensions.libs) requires these
        ;; so the host loads them once and extension contexts share the
        ;; namespaces by reference.
        dev.weavejester/cljfmt {:mvn/version "0.16.6"}
        rewrite-clj/rewrite-clj {:mvn/version "1.3.58"}
        parinferish/parinferish {:mvn/version "0.8.0"}
        borkdude/edamame {:mvn/version "1.6.44"}
        org.clojure/spec.alpha {:mvn/version "0.5.238"}
        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version "1.6.0"}
        ;; SCI: the tool layer's sandbox (tools/run-code) mints its own
        ;; contexts, and the loader's design puts the backend artifact on the
        ;; caller (loader.md §6.5). Same pin as agent's and jolt's.
        org.babashka/sci {:git/url "https://github.com/yogthos/sci.git"
                          :git/sha "1295142fc29f206dd2747963548ba038077d9205"}}}
